00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:21,080
So let's prepare a welcoming
party for them, shall we?

268
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,017
Hey, Mama.

269
00:21:23,100 --> 00:21:26,980
Turns out that cake you want is
in Chocolatown on Cacao Island.

270
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:28,495
Let's head there now.

271
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:32,400
I lickety-like to her out of desperation.

272
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:37,280
But if this plays out, it'll be like
I was telling the truth all along.

273
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:42,296
Pudding is baking the cake
at Cacao Island, after all.

274
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:48,527
This could still go south, but it looks
like the pieces are falling into place.

275
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:01,700
Oh, wedding cat!

276
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:03,530
Over there?

277
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:04,800
You got it!

278
00:22:09,540 --> 00:22:11,320
Stop! No! No!

279
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,720
That's Nuts Island!

280
00:22:13,500 --> 00:22:16,157
Are you guys even lickety-listening to me?

281
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:19,097
That's not where the
wedding cake is going, Mama.

282
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:22,239
We need to head to Cacao
Island or you won't get it.

283
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:24,137
Wedding cake!

284
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:25,840
Yes, yes, but not there.

285
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:28,900
Stop, I'm going to lickety-lose my mind.

286
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,440
He never learns.

287
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:40,380
How about this? Help!

288
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:46,760
Now, Gum-Gum!

289
00:23:11,340 --> 00:23:12,740
Aaaaaaahhh!

290
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:26,083
Uh!

291
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:27,990
Ah!

292
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:46,700
Damn it!

293
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:50,569
He knows exactly where I'm going
to dodge every single time!

294
00:23:51,780 --> 00:23:53,040
Swearing me out!

295
00:23:55,860 --> 00:23:57,580
The feeling is mutual.

296
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:02,520
No one's ever evaded so many
of my attacks for so long.

297
00:24:03,260 --> 00:24:04,420
It's stressful.

298
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:23,120
Were you trying to grab my mole?

299
00:24:25,300 --> 00:24:27,820
Yeah, I'll get it next time for sure.

300
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:30,960
Flowing mochi.

301
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,640
Whoa, what?

302
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,400
We're turned into mochi!

303
00:24:57,920 --> 00:25:01,380
This is just like what Doe Flamingo did!

304
00:25:02,820 --> 00:25:04,840
Listen closely, rookie.

305
00:25:07,340 --> 00:25:10,140
My Devil Fruit's power ascended.

306
00:25:10,380 --> 00:25:12,840
They've reached a new horizon.

307
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:15,200
A higher state known as awakening.

308
00:25:15,800 --> 00:25:18,780
It's only natural that
my ability has awakened.

309
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:27,900
It's no use.

310
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:31,375
And there's no pot of tea to
help you escape this time.

311
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:37,477
I could just chop you up.

312
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:41,340
Or I could let the mochi
suffocate you on its own.

313
00:25:41,660 --> 00:25:43,580
How would you like to die?

314
00:25:44,020 --> 00:25:46,120
I am not gonna die!

315
00:25:49,980 --> 00:25:51,080
Fourth gear.

316
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:53,960
This just got interesting.

317
00:26:05,580 --> 00:26:06,874
Something isn't right.

318
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:13,037
Feels like we should have gotten the
location of Straw Hat's ship by now.

319
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:16,473
Does this mean something
happened to the territory slugs?

320
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,557
Peckhams, that's enough out of you!

321
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,180
Stop your crying already!

322
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:25,380
But I'm sad about Pedro!

323
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:28,760
I'm sympathetic.

324
00:26:29,580 --> 00:26:31,677
Pedro was like a brother to Peckham,

325
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:34,937
so having him meet such an end,
c 'est une tragedy terrible.

326
00:26:35,020 --> 00:26:36,314
What, are you friends?

327
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:38,070
Well...

328
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:41,557
I can't die just yet.

329
00:26:41,640 --> 00:26:43,957
The dawn of the new world is coming soon.

330
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,280
I can't rest until I've seen it!

331
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:52,202
This should be more than enough
to undo all of your little tricks.

332
00:26:52,660 --> 00:26:53,820
That's dynamite!

333
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:56,150
Adios.

334
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:07,540
Friend of all, this came
to me as a bit of a shock.

335
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:11,837
I saw Pedro five years ago.

336
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,257
Fighting part of this part.

337
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,417
To hold on to every moment of his life.

338
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:16,980
That my mom might spare.

339
00:27:17,680 --> 00:27:19,477
It's that same man was willing.

340
00:27:19,560 --> 00:27:21,497
To sacrifice his life and on his tongue.

341
00:27:21,580 --> 00:27:23,197
To help the Straw Hats.

342
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:25,045
You getting at something here?

343
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:32,685
Perhaps we're making an error.

344
00:27:33,320 --> 00:27:37,937
After all, there are many who have paid
the price for underestimating Straw Hat.

345
00:27:38,020 --> 00:27:39,373
What are you proposing?

346
00:27:39,700 --> 00:27:42,737
Simply that we should be
more cautious on this matter.

347
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:44,620
Mama won't lose to some brat.

348
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:49,397
You're implying that Straw Hat is
so weak that it's part dangerous?

349
00:27:49,480 --> 00:27:50,480
Compared to Mama?

350
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:52,602
Straw Hat is nothing but a joke.

351
00:27:54,060 --> 00:27:58,020
Now, you would still say that
looking at the state of the Shit?

352
00:27:58,300 --> 00:28:00,040
Clearly that was an accident!

353
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:01,772
And the territory slugs!

354
00:28:02,020 --> 00:28:06,079
Is it an accident as well that
they're failing to function right now?

355
00:28:07,940 --> 00:28:08,770
What?

356
00:28:08,853 --> 00:28:10,737
You think they planned all of this?

357
00:28:10,820 --> 00:28:12,617
That we're playing into some trap?

358
00:28:12,700 --> 00:28:13,935
I'll put it this way.

359
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:19,029
En Serious, unexpected incidents has
been occurring ever since they got here.

360
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:25,900
A champion's pride comes before a fall.

361
00:28:26,600 --> 00:28:30,480
Is it not our job to protect
Mama's honor? Therefore,

362
00:28:30,740 --> 00:28:32,517
in order to prevent further accidents,

363
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:36,365
let us dispatch a fleet to protect
the borders of our territory.

364
00:28:49,420 --> 00:28:51,477
Excuse me, Mondore? What?

365
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:54,266
The Lady Custard would
like to speak with you.

366
00:28:54,400 --> 00:28:57,047
Custard was chasing
after Veggie, wasn't she?

367
00:28:58,180 --> 00:28:59,700
Yes, this is Mondore.

368
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:02,357
You would better have
some good news for me.

369
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:03,270
Wow!

370
00:29:05,080 --> 00:29:08,980
The thing is, we lost
Veggie's ship. You won!

371
00:29:09,260 --> 00:29:13,960
For some reason, the territory slugs
aren't sending us its location. Great.

372
00:29:14,280 --> 00:29:15,840
It's not just us. What?

373
00:29:16,040 --> 00:29:17,937
We were trying to drag Straw Hat's ship,

374
00:29:18,020 --> 00:29:20,317
and the damn territory slugs
weren't giving us a thing!

375
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:21,480
Are you serious?

376
00:29:21,980 --> 00:29:25,100
Just go and look for
Veggie on your own. Do not.

377
00:29:25,300 --> 00:29:28,180
And I repeat, do not
let him escape. Got it.

378
00:29:28,840 --> 00:29:29,670
Click.

379
00:29:29,753 --> 00:29:32,980
Hey, go check on them right away. On who?

380
00:29:33,240 --> 00:29:34,917
What the hell do you
think I'm talking about

381
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:37,117
on the territory slugs screwing us over?

382
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:38,560
Yes, sir. Damn it.

383
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:40,704
I'll get to the bottom of this.

384
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:49,459
Didn't think they'd give
up the chase quite so easy.

385
00:29:49,620 --> 00:29:51,032
Wonder what the deal is.

386
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:55,257
Maybe the territory slugs don't know
where we're trying to go, little old.

387
00:29:55,340 --> 00:29:57,540
Are they jammed or what? Dunno.

388
00:29:57,980 --> 00:30:00,057
But if they were operating like usual,

389
00:30:00,140 --> 00:30:02,357
then our transponder
snails would be reacting,

390
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:03,270
wouldn't they?

391
00:30:03,353 --> 00:30:05,557
Maybe they're sleeping
on the job, little old.

392
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:06,470
You think so?

393
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:09,151
I've never heard of that happening before.

394
00:30:09,320 --> 00:30:11,020
I'm not complaining, though.

395
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,300
Let's keep hauling ass, boys.

396
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:16,757
My lady is waiting for me.

397
00:30:16,840 --> 00:30:20,800
Head this ship straight to Cacao
Island to be quick about it!

398
00:30:49,140 --> 00:30:52,260
This is Nasorta calling from Jerma's ship.

399
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:53,617
How'd the battle go?

400
00:30:53,700 --> 00:30:54,530
Good news?

401
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:58,600
We marched in with 10,000
soldiers and crushed them.

402
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,527
Their kingdom is devastated.

403
00:31:01,660 --> 00:31:02,860
That's my brother.

404
00:31:03,120 --> 00:31:04,238
You had me worried.

405
00:31:05,560 --> 00:31:06,501
Are you kidding?

406
00:31:06,780 --> 00:31:07,820
Jerma's nothing.

407
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:10,100
With our strength, it was easy.

408
00:31:10,740 --> 00:31:12,093
Quick question, though.

409
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:17,980
You didn't destroy the manufacturing
system for the clones, did you?

410
00:31:19,340 --> 00:31:21,200
Course not. Don't you worry.

411
00:31:21,580 --> 00:31:23,345
I know that was our objective.

412
00:31:23,440 --> 00:31:26,120
But other than that, the place is wrecked.

413
00:31:28,240 --> 00:31:29,840
As it should be, brother.

414
00:31:30,380 --> 00:31:34,556
Those chair-ma-grunts were doomed
the moment we had them in our sights.

415
00:31:34,660 --> 00:31:37,425
What's going on with
Strawhead and his friends?

416
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:39,340
It's a mess.

417
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:40,797
They made it out to sea.

418
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:43,240
They're trying to escape to the west.

419
00:31:44,800 --> 00:31:46,240
Well, it's no matter.

420
00:31:46,500 --> 00:31:47,857
We'll catch them soon enough.

421
00:31:47,940 --> 00:31:50,175
I'll leave that in your capable hands.

422
00:31:50,640 --> 00:31:52,380
Thanks, and nice work.

423
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:53,950
Click.

424
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,200
Wow, that was pretty easy.

425
00:31:57,600 --> 00:31:59,120
Well, that's good news.

426
00:31:59,460 --> 00:32:00,560
Luffy is safe.

427
00:32:00,900 --> 00:32:01,820
What's next?

428
00:32:02,040 --> 00:32:03,805
There's nothing tying us down.

429
00:32:07,640 --> 00:32:08,740
Set sail.

430
00:32:09,020 --> 00:32:10,220
You know where.

431
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:12,060
Roger that.

432
00:32:13,840 --> 00:32:15,580
Muscle balloon!

433
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:37,360
I tire of watching this
meaningless future play out.

434
00:32:39,860 --> 00:32:42,440
Why should I allow you to power up?

435
00:32:51,580 --> 00:32:53,520
Listen up, Straw Hat!

436
00:32:55,900 --> 00:33:00,020
From now on, I won't underestimate you.

437
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:12,600
Mirror Moshi!

438
00:33:13,120 --> 00:33:14,880
The ceiling spoke to you too?

439
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:18,957
Crap, if that comes down on me,
I'm going to be buried alive!

440
00:33:19,040 --> 00:33:20,880
Yes, you'll suffocate.

441
00:33:22,020 --> 00:33:23,460
Finally, it ends.

442
00:33:41,980 --> 00:33:46,862
Sorry to kill you in such an undignified
manner, but I was getting a bit impatient,

443
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:47,870
you see.

444
00:33:47,953 --> 00:33:52,057
Since you gave me so much trouble, I'm
40 minutes late for today's merienda,

445
00:33:52,140 --> 00:33:53,258
my afternoon snack.

446
00:33:57,940 --> 00:33:59,920
Your suffering will end soon.

447
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:05,160
This is goodbye, Straw Hat.
